{
  "_comment": [
    "Curated seed list for soundtrack_discovery.py. Add entries here, never in code.",
    "",
    "titles[]: name (required), category (required: game|anime|movie|tv),",
    "  aliases (optional), ambiguous (optional, default false).",
    "",
    "  The seed's category is inherited by the ASINs it finds, but only once the",
    "  product proves it is a soundtrack — Amazon's search is fuzzy and returns",
    "  records that merely resemble the query, so matching a seed proves nothing",
    "  on its own. name + aliases also double as the classifier vocabulary that",
    "  categorises label-sourced ASINs.",
    "",
    "  ambiguous: set true when the name is also an ordinary word or a common",
    "  album title — 'Doom', 'Journey', 'Portal', 'Psycho', 'Bleach'. The seed is",
    "  still searched normally; it is only kept out of the classifier vocabulary,",
    "  where it would tag unrelated records (Nirvana's 'Bleach' is not an anime",
    "  OST). Cost of setting it is near zero: a real OST found by that seed still",
    "  proves itself by saying 'soundtrack'/'OST'/'trilha sonora' in its title.",
    "  When in doubt, set it — a missed category is recoverable by enrichment, a",
    "  wrong one pollutes a genre page.",
    "",
    "labels[]: name (required). Boutique OST pressers. No category — they press",
    "  film, game and anime scores mixed, so their ASINs get 'soundtrack' plus",
    "  whatever the title cross-check can prove.",
    "",
    "Seeds rotate by recent yield (see soundtrack_seed_state); adding an entry",
    "here is enough — it gets picked up on the next run with NULL last_searched_at."
  ],

